# Firebase Configuration for Gymnation (project: body-fit-a1823)
#
# Setup for teammates:
#   cp .env.example .env
#   npm install
#   npm run dev
#
# Without a .env file, import.meta.env.VITE_FIREBASE_* is undefined and
# src/firebase.js initialises with an empty config — bookings will fail to
# save to Firestore.
#
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# WHY REAL VALUES ARE COMMITTED HERE
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Firebase *web* config is public by design. Vite inlines every VITE_* variable
# into the production bundle, so these values are already visible to anyone who
# opens the site and views the JavaScript. Google documents this: the API key
# identifies the project, it does not grant access.
#
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# WHAT ACTUALLY SECURES THE DATA — DO THIS BEFORE GOING LIVE
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# 1. Firestore Security Rules. If the database is still in test mode, ANYONE
#    can read and write every booking — member names, phone numbers, emails.
#    Lock the `bookings` collection down in the Firebase console.
# 2. Restrict the API key to your own domains (Google Cloud Console →
#    Credentials → HTTP referrers), so it cannot be used from other sites.
#
# Optional: email confirmations (see src/utils/bookingNotifications.js)
#   VITE_EMAILJS_SERVICE_ID=
#   VITE_EMAILJS_TEMPLATE_ID=
#   VITE_EMAILJS_PUBLIC_KEY=
# Optional: SMS endpoint — must be your own server, never a raw provider key
#   VITE_SMS_ENDPOINT=

VITE_FIREBASE_API_KEY=AIzaSyC8YVZcgktJamYJR4YTMaC2R9nxWtVKyS8
VITE_FIREBASE_AUTH_DOMAIN=body-fit-a1823.firebaseapp.com
VITE_FIREBASE_PROJECT_ID=body-fit-a1823
VITE_FIREBASE_STORAGE_BUCKET=body-fit-a1823.firebasestorage.app
VITE_FIREBASE_MESSAGING_SENDER_ID=839012042785
VITE_FIREBASE_APP_ID=1:839012042785:web:d65b55b5f5525f3d72fb60
VITE_FIREBASE_MEASUREMENT_ID=G-4ND6FQ5NBJ
